\n\nProposed bound: one FIFO of at most4096 reusable subject records, covering every kind. Keep per-input mine records intact, including unknown answers and their retained bytes; use them for that input exactly as today. On insertion of a new reusable name at capacity, drop its oldest reusable entry. Keep updating the same Seen object’s last/prior for every in-flight input that still holds it. A later miss reads Membership/rules again. Do not add a refusal or a signer-key charge at the cache bound. The fold’s highest-head and normal observation guards still apply. Existing active input records do not disappear on eviction.\n\nThis preserves an act naming a real member when the new read answers the same state, and it prevents absent-member floods from consuming admission places. It cannot preserve your unconditional same-outcome sentence in every environment: main can accept on a cached active answer inside300s while a fresh read after eviction is unavailable or reports that member removed. Retaining all such reusable answers is incompatible with a fixed bound under unlimited churn, unless we add another bounded guarantee or durable backing. Dropping only unknown or removed answers also changes reuse/read availability and does not by itself bound the live cached-active history.\n\nPlease rule: accept FIFO4096 with this explicit fresh-read boundary, preserving current input custody and real-member outcomes when the trusted read remains available and unchanged, or require another design that preserves all current grace/reuse outcomes. I will keep R3b source untouched until your ruling and R3a’s review request. The witness will exceed4096 distinct absent members through actual signed Native acts, inspect the real map size, then admit a real member with its original outcome; one control restores today’s unbounded insertion. Additional custody/eviction coverage will follow the ruling. R3b does not hold phase2.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on the concrete R3b bounded-cache 